-- pointing at things, the way §13 describes
  pulse gutter (source) for 1200ms
  highlight run_button (control)
  focus name_field (control)
  reveal results (pane)
  annotate editor (source) at 12-18
  annotate editor (source) at 7

-- a bad widget name LISTS the real ones, so a model can correct itself
  refused: no widget named "run_panel"; there is browser, tabs, editor, gutter, run_strip, output, results, branches, tables, assistant, name_field, run_button, save_button, new_file_button, new_folder_button, overlay_strip

-- so does a bad gesture
  refused: no gesture named "wiggle"; there is highlight, pulse, focus, reveal, annotate

-- and a gesture a widget cannot perform says what it can
  refused: browser is a pane, which cannot annotate; it can highlight, pulse, reveal
  refused: results is a pane, which cannot focus; it can highlight, pulse, reveal

-- focus and highlight are not interchangeable: one takes the keyboard
   away from someone mid-sentence, which is why a pane cannot focus.
